# Task 014 P4: the shell's overlays on layout tokens. Review only (no goldens): the launcher toast at home, over the
# Settings header and over the Calculator; the native hold-Esc ribbon (the toast with its text); the media OSD of the
# brightness / volume keys and the "Loading..." overlay on the native display and over a compat page, the OSD and the loading overlay first made on the compat window and then shown at home again (they follow
# the default display); last the compat ribbon over a stock app (compat numbers, unchanged).
# Compat (display of at most 320 px wide) numbers are today's; the native display gets the DECK / COMPACT tables or
# the token sizes (cp0_ui_overlay.h).
title overlays
review
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
toast "Connected to Home Wi-Fi"
shot ov_toast_home
toast "Bluetooth keyboard connected\nM4 keyboard"
shot ov_toast_home_two_lines
toast off
launch Settings
toast "Wi-Fi: wrong password"
shot ov_toast_settings
toast off
key ESC
launch Calculator
toast "Hold ESC 3s to return home"
shot ov_ribbon_calculator
toast off
key ESC
# a compat page first (the compat window is the default display): the OSD and the overlay are made there
compatpage
osd level Brightness 60
shot ov_osd_level_compat
osd mute on
shot ov_osd_mute_compat
loading "Loading..."
shot ov_loading_compat
loading off
# back at home: they follow the default display
home
osd level Brightness 60
shot ov_osd_level_home
osd level Volume 85
shot ov_osd_volume_home
osd mute on
shot ov_osd_mute_home
wait 1200
loading "Loading..."
shot ov_loading_home
loading off
stockapp
ribbon
shot ov_ribbon_stockapp
